  "_comment_1": "INERT UNTIL THE ROOT IS RE-WATCHED. watchman reads .watchmanconfig at WATCH TIME. /home/newton/work/dev-hermit is already watched, so this file changes nothing today: 'watchman get-config /home/newton/work/dev-hermit' returned {} both before and after it was added. Activation requires 'watchman watch-del' + re-watch, which invalidates a cache shared by every consumer on this box and forces a full re-crawl. That is deliberately DEFERRED to a task gated on the fleet being quiet -- it is scheduled, not forgotten.",
  "_comment_2": "WHY: watchman recursively crawls ~1.7 TB of worktrees/, which is machine-local disposable build trees and already gitignored (.gitignore:24). Each re-crawl (recrawl_count was 46) transiently opens fds inside slot directories. release-worktree.rs's post-fence occupancy check samples /proc for cwd/exe/root/fd/maps and correctly refuses when it sees one -- so a release's own quarantine churn made watchman look like a live occupant and the tool blocked itself. Recorded instance: 'post-fence live process ownership ... pid 702164 fd/187=.../target/debug/deps', where pid 702164 is watchman.",
